Drop redundant SymbolDeclaredTwice eqlog check

`resolve_scopes` already detects duplicate decl-level symbols via
`insert_decl_symbol` and bails on the first conflict, well before
`check_eqlog` runs. The eqlog-side `iter_symbol_declared_twice_errors`
in `eqlog/src/semantics/mod.rs` was therefore unreachable for any
program reaching that pass.

Remove the iter and its entry in `check_eqlog`. The
`accessible_symbol` machinery in `eqlog.eql` stays — it's still needed
by `iter_symbol_lookup_errors` for `UndeclaredSymbol`/`BadSymbolKind`.

The two `symbol_declared_twice_*` compile-error tests continue to pass
unchanged, served entirely by the Rust-side scope pass.
